# Build context of the ONE container definition of this repository:
#   scripts/host/container/Dockerfile.ubuntu-24.04   (task 4 blueprint row 78; README beside it)
# The context is the repository root, so this file has to lie here: the docker client installed on the
# development Mac has no buildx plugin, and its builder reads no ignore file beside a Dockerfile.
#
# FORM: an allow list. Everything is excluded, then three folders are let in, then the exclusions that
# must hold INSIDE and BESIDE them are stated again by name, so that widening the allow list later cannot
# let them in by accident. The last matching line wins.
*
!apps
apps/*
!apps/capture-worker
!scripts
scripts/*
!scripts/host
!scripts/hardware-acceptance

# Never sent, whatever the allow list above becomes:
apps/input-av
apps/input-av/**
**/node_modules
.data
**/.data
.cache
**/.cache
docs
.git
.locks
**/.env
**/.env.*

# This Mac's build output (Mach-O binaries, scratch files of the unit checks): the container builds its own.
apps/capture-worker/build
**/__pycache__
**/.DS_Store
